A||||13||mrtgman||Looking for cool fuel door ideas...||||1||
Z||000000||mrtgman||12-06-2001||11:32 PM||||I am looking for ideas to replace the existing fuel door on my 86 gt. Something like the Audi TT or eclipse look without too many modifications. Anyone know of any that are basically a perfect fit?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierofront1_1.jpg">   86 gt owned since new!<A HREF="http://www.palmbeachloan.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.palmbeachloan.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MikeSchaefer||12-06-2001||11:48 PM||||My Fiero has a harley gas filler on it and looks cool as hell, but there is quite a bit of modifying needed in order to do this<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.soulshadow.com/new2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.soulshadow.com/thumb7gasopen.jpg">   <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.soulshadow.com/thumb6gascap1.jpg">   <BR>there are some more pics on my site: <A HREF="http://www.soulshadow.com/myride.html" TARGET=_blank>Worldwide Fiero Links</A> <BR>Mike Schaefer<P>[This message has been edited by MikeSchaefer (edited 12-06-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by MikeSchaefer (edited 12-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||rodmcneill||12-07-2001||12:34 AM||||Doni Hagan that is on this forum did something like that to his Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||12-07-2001||10:36 AM||||Yeah, Doni's car utilized extensive modifications... it's called a "<B>sticker</B>"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> read about it here: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010559.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010559.html</A> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GAS_DOOR.jpg"> <P>I have the parts to do a conversion using the door from the Izuzu Vehicross... but it too will take a fair amount of mods.  The one for the audi TT is extremely expensive and too rounded, the one from an eclipse is too large.  I checked for motorcycle parts... they <I>might</I> work.  Otherwise the Vehicross parts are just slightly larger than the existing opening (when you remove the current cup/door assembly) and only run around $85.  I probably won't get around to trying to install it until sometime next year!<P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||12-07-2001||10:42 AM||||I didn't change the door, but I like the look when the ring is painted black.<P><BR>Phil started the craze  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1249362&a=9233482&p=30056864&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||7
