Z||000010||REDHOTT88||12-07-2001||06:50 PM||||Fotofrank,<P>Where did you find that on the website?<P>I have the catalog, but it is not listed... <P>I think that looks good! And it's 1/2 the price of what Doni paid!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red and shiny all over!)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000011||MinnGreenGT||12-07-2001||08:26 PM||||RedHott88... they're listed in JC Whitney's Sport & Compact section.  Try the website: <A HREF="http://www.jcwsportcompact.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jcwsportcompact.com</A>   and look for stock numbers: 47XU3338W (5.2" round), 47XU3339U (4.76" round), 47XU3340B (4.33" round), or 47XU3341P (5.75"x4.5" rectangle)<BR>They're all listed at $12.99<P>BTW: I may still have to get one from Doni... just 'cause it says "green car" on it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||fotofrank||12-08-2001||12:31 AM||||Yep MinnGreen is correct. They are in the Sport and Compact catalog. I measured my gas cover at 5.0 inches so this is what we need: 47XU3338W (5.2" round) The extra 0.20 inches can be easily trimmed,if needed but I feel that the ring around the gas cover is greater than 5.0 inches. So it will fit. Remember it is round so the size is only 0.10 inches on each edge. So should I get one and will other Fiero owners point and laugh?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> I have given this idea much thought  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE<p>[This message has been edited by fotofrank (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000013||MikeSchaefer||12-08-2001||12:49 AM||||I didn't do the harley mod myself, but I know the basics of what's involved with the mod:  The first thing that was done was cutting a new hole for where the new gas filler will go, and then glassing over the old one.  Then the gas line was rerouted to the new hole, and one of those cool fast-fill nozzles was put on underneath it (so you don't need a cap.<BR>   I know that is making it seem like a small task, but it does take a little work, if you used filler and had someone to paint it for you, it would probably be pretty cheap though.  <BR><B>GtFiero1</B>: I'll never give out the details of how to attach Mr. Fusion to the fiero though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Good luck,<BR>Mike<BR>||||reg||6
